 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F G : Points
AB ⟂ BC [00]
AD ∥ BC [01]
AB ∥ CD [02]
E,D,B are collinear [03]
A,E,C are collinear [04]
E,F,D are collinear [05]
FE = FD [06]
G,E,A are collinear [07]
GE = GA [08]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. AB ⟂ BC [00] & BC ∥ AD [01] & AB ∥ CD [02] ⇒  ∠BAD = ∠BCD [09]
002. ∠BAD = ∠BCD [09] ⇒  A,D,C,B are concyclic [10]
003. A,D,C,B are concyclic [10] ⇒  ∠ADB = ∠ACB [11]
004. F,E,D are collinear [05] & FE = FD [06] ⇒  F is midpoint of ED [12]
005. G,E,A are collinear [07] & GE = GA [08] ⇒  G is midpoint of EA [13]
006. F is midpoint of ED [12] & G is midpoint of EA [13] ⇒  FG ∥ DA [14]
007. E,F,D are collinear [05] & E,D,B are collinear [03] & G,E,A are collinear [07] & A,E,C are collinear [04] & ∠ADB = ∠ACB [11] & FG ∥ AD [14] & AD ∥ BC [01] ⇒  ∠GFB = ∠GCB [15]
008. ∠GFB = ∠GCB [15] ⇒  G,F,C,B are concyclic [16]
009. E,F,D are collinear [05] & E,D,B are collinear [03] & G,E,A are collinear [07] & A,E,C are collinear [04] & ∠ADB = ∠ACB [11] & FG ∥ AD [14] & AD ∥ BC [01] ⇒  ∠GFB = ∠CGF [17]
010. G,F,C,B are concyclic [16] & ∠GFB = ∠CGF [17] ⇒  GB = CF
